 estate business with a $1.1B market cap on $336M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 14.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 5.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.05273548368751741},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 22% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(DEA) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/DEA_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111026050401_1794348241.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794348241.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Easterly Government Properties, Inc. (NYSE:DEA) Stock Has Consensus Target Price of $25.60","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/easterly-government-properties-inc-nysedea-stock-has-consensus-target-price-of-25-60.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794311946.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Easterly Government Properties (DEA) Updates Guidance On A Valuation Narrative Still Under Review","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-dea/easterly-government-properties/news/easterly-government-properties-dea-updates-guidance-on-a-val","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794191108.072,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Is Easterly Government Properties (DEA) Trading At A Premium After Results?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-dea/easterly-government-properties/news/is-easterly-government-properties-dea-trading-at-a-premium-a","date":"202